  "trendsDeltaHint": "The odd one out: sideways is the charge level, not time. Each dot is one reading, placed by how full the pack was and how far apart its highest and lowest cell were at that moment. What matters is the shape. Flat across the middle with a spike near full is one cell with less capacity than the rest. A curve that follows the current instead, higher under load, is resistance somewhere, and almost always a connection rather than a cell.",
